# Deployment & Hosting Guide

Your application is ready for production! Here is the recommended path for hosting:

## 1. Database (MongoDB Atlas)
Since you are currently using a local MongoDB, you'll need a cloud instance:
1. Create a free account at [MongoDB Atlas](https://www.mongodb.com/cloud/atlas).
2. Create a new cluster and get your `CONNECTION_STRING`.
3. Whitelist `0.0.0.0/0` (or the specific IPs of your hosting providers) in the network access settings.

## 2. Backend (Render / Railway)
Render is a great free/cheap option for Node.js:
1. Push your code to a GitHub repository.
2. Connect your GitHub to [Render](https://render.com/).
3. Create a new **Web Service**.
4. Set the **Root Directory** to `./`.
5. Set the **Build Command** to `npm install`.
6. Set the **Start Command** to `node src/server.js`.
7. **CRITICAL**: Add all your [.env](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/OneDrive/Desktop/fullauth/.env) variables in the "Environment" tab on Render.

## 3. Frontend (Vercel / Netlify)
Vercel is optimized for Vite/React:
1. Connect your GitHub to [Vercel](https://vercel.com/).
2. Import the project.
3. Set the **Root Directory** to `client/`.
4. Vercel will auto-detect Vite. The build command is `npm run build` and output directory is `dist`.
5. Add any frontend environment variables (like `VITE_API_URL` if you use one) in the Vercel dashboard.

## 🚀 Pushing to GitHub
Yes, you can push the code now!
```bash
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit: FullAuth with Premium UI and OTP"
git push origin main
```
> [!IMPORTANT]
> Your [.env](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/OneDrive/Desktop/fullauth/.env) file is already in [.gitignore](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/OneDrive/Desktop/fullauth/.gitignore), so it won't be pushed. This is correct for security. You must manually add those secrets to your hosting provider's dashboard.

## Production Checklist
- [ ] Update `baseURL` in [client/src/api/auth.js](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/OneDrive/Desktop/fullauth/client/src/api/auth.js) to your deployed backend URL.
- [ ] Ensure `EMAIL_PASS` (App Password) is kept secret.
- [ ] Change `JWT_SECRET` to a long, random string for production.
